<table border="0" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="100%"><tr><td>
<a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=6"><img src="images/topics/magazines.gif" border="0" Alt="Magazines" align="right" hspace="10" vspace="10"></a>
<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>, 45, "wants to open her own management company to 
manage other forms of talents besides singers," says a source. The 
<STRONG>Maverick Records</STRONG> label that she founded in home to 
<STRONG>Alanis Morissette</STRONG> and <STRONG>Michelle Branch</STRONG>, but 
according to an insider, "<STRONG>she'd also like to manage the careers of 
directors, music video directors, choreographers and actors</STRONG>." She even 
wants to represent writers like <STRONG>Deepak Chopra</STRONG>, who will be at 
her Passover seders in <STRONG>L.A.</STRONG> on April 5 and 6, the source say. 
The source says that the <STRONG>Material Girl</STRONG>, who reportedly will 
perform in <STRONG>Israel</STRONG> on her summer <STRONG>Re-Invention world 
tour</STRONG> starting May 24, has seen "how much money <STRONG>Deepak</STRONG> 
has made, for example, and sees it as a great opportunity." And on the subject 
of her tour, last week <STRONG>"Star People"</STRONG> broke exclusively that 
<STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> was going to do a documentary, like her <STRONG>"True 
Or Dare"</STRONG> film. Now <STRONG>"Star People"</STRONG> hears she's also 
negotiating a TV special this summer. "It will be a broadcast of the concert on 
<STRONG>HBO</STRONG>," the source says.<br><br><b>Note:</b> <i>Source: <STRONG>Star People</STRONG>. Special thanks to our friend <STRONG>Jeannie</STRONG> at <STRONG><A href="http://www.madonnasworld.com" target=_blank>Madonna's World</A></STRONG>. </i>

</font></div>
</td></tr></table>


