<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><P><STRONG>It seems that more videos&nbsp;for Madonna's upcoming shows will be filmed&nbsp;besides the two we previously reported as being already shot.</STRONG></P>
<P><STRONG>Robster </STRONG>from <STRONG>madonnamadforum</STRONG> exclusively revealed the following info about the video footage will be used in the video projections of the tour:</P>
<P><SPAN id=postcolor><FONT color=#000000>Hi there,<BR><BR>We have just received information from an anonymous source which reveals information for parts to be cast for use in videos shot in mid April. The video footage will be used in the video projections of the tour! Here is a breakdown of the parts being cast according to this source:<BR><BR><B>* Real Mom 20ish with son age 4ish, African American<BR>* Real Mom 2 35ish with son age 13ish, African American<BR>* Real Moms or Dads 30s with real sons or daughters age 5-6, African American<BR><BR>more info on the general idea they have for the parts to be cast:<BR><BR>This takes place during 1965, the Voting Rights Act, Civil Rights, Malcolm X, Martin Luther King, Jr, Selma to Montgomery March, Black Panthers era in the deep south...<BR>We need that look - not the contemporary dreadlocks, braids and stuff, and the kids those days were not mixed race.<BR>It's 1965...<BR>The word African American hasn't even evolved yet.<BR><BR>some other info on the final way to decide the final core group of dancers. Madonna apparently used a tactic to make her final pick. She had all of the dancers tell a joke! If they made her laugh they were in, if not...they were out!</B><BR><BR>This is all the information the source could give me at this time!<BR><BR>ROB :: posted on april 3rd 2004</FONT> </SPAN><SPAN><!--Signature--><BR><STRONG><EM>Thanks to our friend Robster.</EM></STRONG></SPAN></P>
</font></div>
</td></tr></table>


