<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000">Our member <STRONG>Dave C</STRONG> sent us a reportage of his "tickets day." He tells how he got tickets for <STRONG>London Wembley Arena</STRONG> venues. <BR><BR><EM>It was great at <STRONG>Wembley</STRONG>. Today I stayed out for 24 hours to get a front row ticket and I got one. <BR>The staff was very good and made sure all the REAL fans got the best tickets and the touts had the bad ones. <BR>Then I went away for a hour then went back to the box office and got the next date 23 in AA ROW 13. I WAS SO HAPPY LIKE MY FRIENDS. <BR>Then I waited for one more hour and got the 3rd night AA front row from the box office. I could not believe my luck. <BR>Not a lot of fans went down to <STRONG>Wembley</STRONG>. I don't know why. It was the best way to get great tickets. <BR>From a very happy <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> fan can't wait for the tour now.</EM> 
</font></div>
